{
  "title": "NeuroGen Corp Negotiation Package Preparation",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nThis plan constructs a comprehensive negotiation package for the NeuroGen Corp licensing deal across four parallel workstreams, then synthesizes everything into a final deliverable.\n\n### Workstreams:\n1. **Technical Dossier** - Crystal structures, SAR data, 200-compound pilot results synthesis\n2. **Term Sheet Framework** - Licensing terms prioritizing speed (12mo), cost (€2.5M cap), IP (CNS-only exclusivity)\n3. **Equity-for-Speed Proposal** - 5% equity (€2.5M at €50M pre-money) for 3-month acceleration, with valuation justification\n4. **Fallback Position Matrix** - Tiered concessions: equity escalation (→7.5%), timeline extension (→15mo), budget ceiling (→€2.75M), with red lines on IP scope\n5. **Final Assembly** - Synthesize all components into a cohesive, presentation-ready negotiation package\n\nUncertainty is low (deal parameters are well-defined), so we parallelize the four content workstreams and join with a synthesis step.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Build the Technical Dossier section of the negotiation package. Using the uploaded data files, create a professional technical dossier covering: (1) Crystal Structure Summary - synthesize the co-crystal PDB data, CryoEM 2.9Å model refinement notes, binding site residues/contacts/waters from Structure_Summary_Table.xlsx into an executive summary with key structural insights for NeuroGen; (2) SAR Analysis - analyze SAR_MasterTable_v7.xlsx to identify potency trends, selectivity profiles, key pharmacophore features, and top lead compounds with IC50/EC50 values; (3) 200-Compound Pilot Results - synthesize screening results highlighting hit rates, lead series, ADME properties, and PK/PD signals. Format as a polished markdown document suitable for a biotech deal room. Include data tables, key findings, and strategic implications for CNS drug development.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Draft a comprehensive Term Sheet Framework for licensing deal with NeuroGen Corp. Structure: (1) DEAL TYPE: Technology license with partnership option; (2) SPEED: 12-month project timeline with milestones at 3/6/9/12 months, acceleration clauses, penalty/incentive structure for timeline adherence; (3) COST: €2.5M total cap with payment structure (upfront, milestone-based, success fees), clear budget allocation across workstreams, cost overrun provisions; (4) IP RIGHTS: CNS-only exclusivity granted to NeuroGen, all non-CNS rights retained by licensor, field-of-use definitions, sublicensing terms, IP ownership of improvements/derivatives, publication rights; (5) GOVERNANCE: Joint steering committee, decision-making framework, dispute resolution; (6) TERMINATION: Material breach, convenience termination, IP reversion clauses. Use standard biotech licensing language. Output as professional markdown term sheet.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Structure the Equity-for-Speed Proposal for NeuroGen Corp. Create a detailed proposal document covering: (1) CORE OFFER: 5% equity stake in our company offered to NeuroGen in exchange for 3-month timeline acceleration (12→9 months); (2) VALUATION MATH: Pre-money valuation €50M, 5% = €2.5M equity value, explain value proposition and upside for NeuroGen; (3) EQUITY MECHANICS: Share class, vesting schedule tied to acceleration milestones, anti-dilution provisions, board observer rights if any, tag-along/drag-along; (4) ACCELERATION REQUIREMENTS: Define what '3-month acceleration' means operationally - specific deliverables, resource commitments from NeuroGen, dedicated team requirements; (5) PERFORMANCE CONDITIONS: Equity vests only if acceleration milestones are met, clawback provisions if timeline slips back; (6) STRATEGIC RATIONALE: Why this is win-win - NeuroGen gets upside in platform beyond CNS deal, we get speed-to-market advantage. Output as polished markdown proposal document.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Create the Fallback Position Matrix and Negotiation Strategy document for NeuroGen Corp deal. Include: (1) FALLBACK TIER 1 - Equity Adjustment: Increase from 5% to up to 7.5% equity (€3.75M value at €50M pre-money), conditions under which to offer this, what to extract in return; (2) FALLBACK TIER 2 - Timeline Extension: Extend from 12 to 15 months (3-month extension), milestone restructuring, how this affects cost and deliverables; (3) FALLBACK TIER 3 (Last Resort) - Budget Increase: Up to €2.75M (€250K increase), justification requirements, scope expansion to justify cost; (4) RED LINES: IP scope is non-negotiable - CNS-only exclusivity must be maintained, no reduction in retained non-CNS rights under any circumstances; (5) NEGOTIATION TACTICS: Opening positions, concession sequencing (equity first, then timeline, budget last), BATNA analysis, NeuroGen's likely pressure points and motivations; (6) DECISION TREE: If-then flowchart for negotiation scenarios. Output as markdown strategy document.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all four components into the final NeuroGen Corp Negotiation Package. Combine: (1) Technical Dossier from Task 0, (2) Term Sheet Framework from Task 1, (3) Equity-for-Speed Proposal from Task 2, (4) Fallback Position Matrix from Task 3. Create a cohesive, professionally structured negotiation package with: Executive Summary (1-page deal overview), Table of Contents, all four sections integrated with consistent formatting and cross-references, Appendices section for raw data references, Key Discussion Points summary for the negotiation meeting, and a Quick Reference Card with deal parameters (€2.5M cap, 12-month timeline, 5% equity, CNS-only exclusivity, fallback thresholds). Ensure internal consistency across all sections and flag any conflicts between components.",
      "tool_name": "reasoning",
      "depends_on": [0, 1, 2, 3]
    }
  ],
